ite towards Energy Storage: Fabrication and Investigation.\u003Cem> Appl. Therm. Eng. \u003C/em>\u003Cstrong>2024\u003C/strong>,\u003Cem> 256\u003C/em>, 124073. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.applthermaleng.2024.124073.\u003C/p>",117,{"id":545,"articleId":5,"doi":48,"fullContent":546,"sort":547},"2059835814045405186","\u003Cp>Dai, L.; Karakas, O.; Cheng, Y.; et al. A Review on Carbon Materials Production from Plastic Wastes.\u003Cem> Chem. Eng. J. \u003C/em>\u003Cstrong>2023\u003C/strong>,\u003Cem> 453\u003C/em>, 139725. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2022.139725.\u003C/p>",118,{"id":549,"articleId":5,"doi":48,"fullContent":550,"sort":551},"2059835814045405187","\u003Cp>Shi, X.; Zhu, J.; Chen, B.; et al. Dissecting the Chemical Strain in Inactive Components of Sodium‑Ion Battery Cathodes.\u003Cem> Scr. Mater. \u003C/em>\u003Cstrong>2025\u003C/strong>,\u003Cem> 268\u003C/em>, 116880. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scriptamat.2025.116880.\u003C/p>",119,{"id":553,"articleId":5,"doi":48,"fullContent":554,"sort":555},"2059835814045405188","\u003Cp>Tewari, C.; Pathak, M.; Tatrari, G.; et al. Waste Plastics Derived Reduced Graphene Oxide‑Based Nanocomposite with Fe\u003Csub>3\u003C/sub>O\u003Csub>4\u003C/sub> for Water Purification and Supercapacitor Applications.\u003Cem> J. Ind. Eng. Chem. \u003C/em>\u003Cstrong>2024\u003C/strong>,\u003Cem> 130\u003C/em>, 346–356. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jiec.2023.09.038.\u003C/p>",120,{"id":557,"articleId":5,"doi":48,"fullContent":558,"sort":559},"2059835814045405189","\u003Cp>Cao, J.; Liang, X.; Ruamruk, S.; et al. Evaporation Cold Energy Storage and Thermoelectric Harvesting via Hydrogel-Phase Change Material-Thermoelectric Generator Tandem Structure.\u003Cem> Small Struct. \u003C/em>\u003Cstrong>2026\u003C/strong>,\u003Cem> 7\u003C/em>, e202500635. https://doi.org/10.1002/sstr.202500635.\u003C/p>",121,{"id":561,"articleId":5,"doi":48,"fullContent":562,"sort":563},"2059835814045405190","\u003Cp>Cheng, S.; Tao, C.; Li, H. Preparation of Carbon Nanotubes from Organic Solid Wastes: A Review.\u003Cem> J. Anal. Appl. Pyrolysis \u003C/em>\u003Cstrong>2025\u003C/strong>,\u003Cem> 192\u003C/em>, 107240. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaap.2025.107240.\u003C/p>",122,{"id":565,"articleId":5,"doi":48,"fullContent":566,"sort":567},"2059835814045405191","\u003Cp>Zhang, Y.; Wang, J.; Yang, X.; et al. Fabrication of Shape-Stabilized Phase Change Materials Based on Waste Plastics for Energy Storage.\u003Cem> J. Energy Storage \u003C/em>\u003Cstrong>2022\u003C/strong>,\u003Cem> 52\u003C/em>, 104973. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.est.2022.104973.\u003C/p>",123,{"id":569,"articleId":5,"doi":48,"fullContent":570,"sort":571},"2059835814045405192","\u003Cp>Teggar, M.; Ajarostaghi, S.S.M.; Yıldız, Ç.; et al. Performance Enhancement of Latent Heat Storage Systems by Using Extended Surfaces and Porous Materials: A State-of-the-Art Review.\u003Cem> J. Energy Storage \u003C/em>\u003Cstrong>2021\u003C/strong>,\u003Cem> 44\u003C/em>, 103340. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.est.2021.103340.\u003C/p>",124,{"id":573,"articleId":5,"doi":48,"fullContent":574,"sort":575},"2059835814045405193","\u003Cp>Xiong, Y.; Zhang, A.; Zhao, Y.; et al. A Mini Review on Sewage Sludge and Red Mud Recycling for Thermal Energy Storage.\u003Cem> Energies \u003C/em>\u003Cstrong>2024\u003C/strong>,\u003Cem> 17\u003C/em>, 2079. https://doi.org/10.3390/en17092079.\u003C/p>",125,{"id":577,"articleId":5,"doi":48,"fullContent":578,"sort":579},"2059835814045405194","\u003Cp>Tian, Y.; Yang, R.; Pan, H.; et al. Biomass-Based Shape-Stabilized Phase Change Materials for Thermal Energy Storage and Multiple Energy Conversion.\u003Cem> Nano Energy \u003C/em>\u003Cstrong>2025\u003C/strong>,\u003Cem> 133\u003C/em>, 110440. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nanoen.2024.110440.\u003C/p>",126,{"id":581,"articleId":5,"doi":48,"fullContent":582,"sort":583},"2059835814045405195","\u003Cp>Jiang, J.; Cao, Y.; Li, G.; et al. Using Industrial Mining Solid Waste through Conversion to Phase-Change Materials for Thermal Energy Storage.\u003Cem> ChemPlusChem \u003C/em>\u003Cstrong>2025\u003C/strong>,\u003Cem> 90\u003C/em>, e202400519. https://doi.org/10.1002/cplu.202400519.\u003C/p>",127,[585,593,599,605,612,619,627],{"id":586,"articleId":5,"userId":48,"firstName":587,"middleName":588,"lastName":589,"suffix":48,"email":590,"superscript":591,"collab":48,"orcid":592,"corresponding":12,"sort":34},"2056199489945718786","Kamal","A. R.","Ismail","kamal@fem.unicamp.br","1,*","0000-0001-7671-1384",{"id":594,"articleId":5,"userId":48,"firstName":595,"middleName":596,"lastName":597,"suffix":48,"email":598,"superscript":18,"collab":48,"orcid":48,"corresponding":23,"sort":70},"2056199489945718787","Fatima","A. M. ","Lino","fatimalino@fem.unicamp.br",{"id":600,"articleId":5,"userId":48,"firstName":601,"middleName":48,"lastName":602,"suffix":48,"email":603,"superscript":19,"collab":48,"orcid":604,"corresponding":23,"sort":90},"2056199489945718788","Aissa ","Atia","a.atia@ens-lagh.dz","0000-0001-6885-3219",{"id":606,"articleId":5,"userId":48,"firstName":607,"middleName":48,"lastName":608,"suffix":48,"email":609,"superscript":610,"collab":48,"orcid":611,"corresponding":23,"sort":94},"2056199489945718789","Abdelghani","Laouer","a_laouer@univ-jijel.dz","3","0000-0003-4996-2668",{"id":613,"articleId":5,"userId":48,"firstName":614,"middleName":48,"lastName":615,"suffix":48,"email":616,"superscript":617,"collab":48,"orcid":618,"corresponding":23,"sort":98},"2056199489945718790","Ameur ","Mechraoui","a.mechraoui@lagh-univ.dz","4","0009-0001-7125-1419",{"id":620,"articleId":5,"userId":48,"firstName":621,"middleName":622,"lastName":623,"suffix":48,"email":624,"superscript":625,"collab":48,"orcid":626,"corresponding":23,"sort":39},"2056199489945718791","Naseer ","H. ","Hamza","naseer.hamza@qu.edu.iq","5","0000-0001-6613-8887",{"id":628,"articleId":5,"userId":48,"firstName":629,"middleName":48,"lastName":630,"suffix":48,"email":631,"superscript":617,"collab":48,"orcid":632,"corresponding":23,"sort":105},"2056199489945718792","Mohamed","Teggar","m.teggar@lagh-univ.dz","0000-0003-3398-9495",[634,637,640,643,646],{"id":635,"articleId":5,"sort":70,"fullContent":636,"country":48,"countryCode":48,"countryAlphaCode":48,"department":48,"institution":48,"city":48,"state":48,"postalCode":48},"2059835813969907713","Energy Department, Faculty of Mechanical Engineering, State University of Campinas, Campinas 13083-860, Brazil",{"id":638,"articleId":5,"sort":90,"fullContent":639,"country":48,"countryCode":48,"countryAlphaCode":48,"department":48,"institution":48,"city":48,"state":48,"postalCode":48},"2059835813969907714","Department of Physics, Higher Normal School of Laghouat, Laghouat 03000, Algeria",{"id":641,"articleId":5,"sort":94,"fullContent":642,"country":48,"countryCode":48,"countryAlphaCode":48,"department":48,"institution":48,"city":48,"state":48,"postalCode":48},"2059835813969907715","Department of Physics, Faculty of Exact Sciences and Computer Science, University of Jijel, Jijel 18000, Algeria",{"id":644,"articleId":5,"sort":98,"fullContent":645,"country":48,"countryCode":48,"countryAlphaCode":48,"department":48,"institution":48,"city":48,"state":48,"postalCode":48},"2059835813969907716","Laboratory of Mechanics, University Amar Telidji, Laghouat 03000, Algeria",{"id":647,"articleId":5,"sort":39,"fullContent":648,"country":48,"countryCode":48,"countryAlphaCode":48,"department":48,"institution":48,"city":48,"state":48,"postalCode":48},"2059835813969907717","Department of Mechanical Engineering, University of Al-Qadisiyah, Ad’Diwaniyah 58001, Iraq",[],[],"\u003Cdiv class=\"csl-right-inline\">\n Ismail, K. A. R.; Lino, F. A. M.; Atia, A.; Laouer, A.; Mechraoui, A.; Hamza, N. H.; Teggar, M. Phase Change Materials from Waste Streams: A Comprehensive Review. \u003Cspan style=\"font-style: italic\">Thermal Science and Applications\u003C/span> \u003Cspan style=\"font-weight: bold\">2026\u003C/span>, \u003Cspan style=\"font-style: italic\">1\u003C/span> (2), 176–199. https://doi.org/10.53941/tsa.2026.100012.\n\u003C/div>","TY  - JOUR\nAU  - Ismail, Kamal A. R.\nAU  - Lino, Fatima A. M.\nAU  - Atia, Aissa\nAU  - Laouer, Abdelghani\nAU  - Mechraoui, Ameur\nAU  - Hamza, Naseer H.\nAU  - Teggar, Mohamed\nPY  - 2026\nTI  - Phase Change Materials from Waste Streams: A Comprehensive Review\nJO  - Thermal Science and Applications\nSP  - 176\nEP  - 199\nVL  - 1\nIS  - 2\nAB  - Phase change materials exhibit high latent heat and nearly isothermal phase change, which make them excellent candidates for many thermal storage as well as cooling applications. Waste generation, on the other hand, is steadily increasing, posing serious management challenges. These wastes are usually rich in chemical elements, oils, and fats and can therefore serve as raw materials for manufacturing valuable chemical products, including PCMs, encapsulations for PCMs, or thermal enhancers for improving heat transfer characteristics of PCMs. Suitable waste materials for the production of PCMs include agricultural and food-processing wastes, such as vegetable oils and fatty acid residues, as well as food-industry by-products. Industrial waste includes materials like polyethylene glycol, polymer processing waste, and industrial by-products. Municipal solid waste can be converted into energy-rich materials and PCMs by adequate thermal and chemical processes. Bio-based PCMs, usually obtained from fatty acids & esters, are derived from waste vegetable oils, animal fats, and food industry byproducts, after being chemically modified via esterification to form effective organic PCMs. Natural waxes are sourced from agricultural residues. Industrial waste-based PCMs are usually obtained from recycled plastics processed by pyrolysis or blended to create composite PCMs. By-products from polymer manufacturing and lost-wax casting wastes can serve as sources for PCMs. Waste-derived PCMs can be incorporated into building components, such as cement mortar, to improve thermal resistance and comfort. Waste-derived PCMs can be used for thermal management in electronics and battery systems to maintain a uniform and acceptable temperature within battery packs. Encapsulated PCMs can be incorporated into fabrics for flexible, medical and protective wearable applications. The continuously expanding application fields of PCMs, such as functional textiles and biomedical applications, require detailed and rigorous characterization of their thermochemical properties, including biodegradability, biosafety, and biocompatibility. This will certainly open new fronts for research and development in the area. The review’s contents can help researchers and professionals involved in waste management and in the development and production of PCMs.\nSN  - 3083-2845\nUR  - https://doi.org/10.53941/tsa.2026.100012\nDO  - 10.53941/tsa.2026.100012\nID  - 2605003961\nER  - ","@article{ismail_lino_atia_laouer_mechraoui_hamza_teggar_2026, title={6cfcd743fe354afcaa1596d999170b54}, volume={1}, ISSN={3083-2845}, DOI={10.53941/tsa.2026.100012}, number={2}, journal={Thermal Science and Applications}, publisher={Scilight Press}, author={Ismail, Kamal A. R. and Lino, Fatima A. M. and Atia, Aissa and Laouer, Abdelghani and Mechraoui, Ameur and Hamza, Naseer H. and Teggar, Mohamed}, year={2026}, pages={176&ndash;199} }",["Reactive",655],{},["Set",657,658],"$aTUEVnxcOx","$m1YbcjGwpF",["ShallowReactive",660],{"/journals/tsa/articles/2605003961-useArticleDetail":48},"/journals/tsa/articles/2605003961",{"useJournalStore":663,"useDeviceStore":783,"usePublisherStore":784},{"journal":664,"journalCode":57,"journalNavBars":688},{"id":13,"fullName":54,"shortName":55,"databaseName":56,"code":57,"logo":48,"cover":58,"backgroundImg":59,"publisher":60,"onlineIssn":61,"printIssn":48,"contactEmail":62,"contactName":63,"articleTotal":64,"publishedArticleCount":65,"pubDate":48,"pubFrequency":48,"themeColor":66,"homeArticleCount":67,"editorEmailVisible":23,"submissionLink":68,"sort":69,"bannerSelected":23,"bannerSort":70,"enabled":12,"citationStyleName":71,"version":72,"createTime":73,"createBy":74,"createByName":75,"updateTime":76,"updateBy":74,"updateByName":77,"twitter":48,"facebook":48,"linkedin":48,"info":665,"indexing":48,"keywords":666,"description":667,"indexingVisible":12,"subjects":668,"editorBoards":676,"currentIssue":677,"forthcomingIssue":685},"\u003Cp style=\"margin-top: 10px;\">\u003Cstrong>Editor-in-Chief: Prof. Marc A. Rosen, Ontario Tech University, Canada.\u003C/strong>\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cem>Thermal Science and Applications\u003C/em>&nbsp;\u003Cem>(TSA)\u003C/em>&nbsp;is an international, peer-reviewed journal dedicated to publishing high-quality research that makes significant advances to the understanding and application of thermal science across a broad range of scientific and engineering disciplines. \u003Ca href=\"/journals/tsa/aimscope\">More\u003C/a>\u003C/p>","Heat and Mass Transfer, Thermodynamics & Energy Conversion, Advanced Thermal Management, Thermal Energy Storage and Sustainability, Renewable and Alternative Thermal Energy Systems, Thermofluids Science and Engineering","This journal seeks to deepen our fundamental understanding of thermal sciences and related phenomena across all scales - from macroscopic energy systems to nanoscale thermal transport mechanisms - while simultaneously driving technological innovation in thermal engineering applications. This includes research to deepen our fundamental understanding of heat transfer and its applications, pioneering work in advanced thermal management solutions for next-generation technologies, transformative approaches to thermal energy conversion and storage, and the development of sustainable thermal systems with low environmental impact. Beyond fundamental research, this journal actively promotes the translation of scientific discoveries into practical engineering applications, serving as a nexus for collaboration between academic researchers and industry practitioner